/-! # Subgroups generated by Galois-stable pointed affine lines

Source: Conrad, The Structure of Solvable Groups over General Fields, proof of
Theorem 2.6, printed p.12; Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), 2.46--2.53 and A.64--A.66.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-galois-stable-affine-line-generated-subgroup)

The affine line over K is the scalar extension of `StandardGroupSchemes.additive k`.
Family stability is expressed by the canonical semilinear squares, using
`baseChangeMap` and `specAlgEquivOver`, with no arbitrary choice of action.
Uniqueness is equality of embedded subgroup schemes, expressed by an isomorphism
commuting with the inclusions into G.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

set_option autoImplicit false

/-- The two clauses of scheme-theoretic generation after extension from k to K:
each affine-line morphism factors through the extended inclusion, and this inclusion
factors through every closed subgroup containing the family. This is a predicate on
actual scheme morphisms, including nonreduced test subgroups.
Source: Conrad, proof of Theorem 2.6, p.12; Milne 2.46--2.51.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-galois-stable-affine-line-generated-subgroup) -/
def IsAffineLineGeneratedAfterBaseChange
    (k K : Type u) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (G : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj G]
    (F : Set
      ((Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj
        (StandardGroupSchemes.additive k) ⟶
       (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj G))
    (L : Over (Spec (.of k))) (i : L ⟶ G) : Prop :=
  (∀ f ∈ F, ∃ g :
      (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj
        (StandardGroupSchemes.additive k) ⟶
      (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj L,
    g ≫ (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).map i = f) ∧
  ∀ (H : Over (Spec (.of K))) (gH : GrpObj H)
    (j : H ⟶ (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj G),
    @IsClosedSubgroupScheme K _ H _ gH
      (Functor.grpObjObj
        (F := Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K))))) j →
    (∀ f ∈ F, ∃ g :
      (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj
        (StandardGroupSchemes.additive k) ⟶ H, g ≫ j = f) →
    ∃ h : (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj L ⟶ H,
      h ≫ j = (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).map i

/-- A Galois-stable set of pointed affine-line morphisms generates a unique smooth
connected closed subgroup over k. The final clause identifies the empty-family result
with the identity subgroup, over the ambient G.
Source: Conrad, proof of Theorem 2.6, p.12, isolated in family form;
Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), 2.46--2.53 and A.64--A.66.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-galois-stable-affine-line-generated-subgroup)

Proof:
1. For a finite subfamily f₁,...,fᵣ use the pointed map on affine 2r-space given by
   a(t)a(s)⁻¹, where a(t)=f₁(t₁)...fᵣ(tᵣ). Swapping t and s inverts its image,
   and setting the other variables to zero recovers each fᵢ. Containment in a closed
   subgroup is therefore equivalent to containing this finite subfamily. Polynomial
   rings over every extension field are domains (lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-domain),
   so these parameter spaces are geometrically reduced and connected, using
   lem-pc-scheme-connected-iff-idempotents. The empty subfamily uses Spec K.
2. Apply lem-sfb-affine-pointed-map-generated-subgroup to each such map. Write I_S
   for the resulting subgroup ideal and put I=intersection I_S. The quotient maps
   from B=O(G_K)/I to B_S=O(G_K)/I_S jointly detect zero.
3. Apply lem-sfb-vector-space-tensor-family-zero-detection to each tensor factor.
   Maps to B_S tensor B_T detect zero; taking U containing S and T shows the diagonal
   maps do too. The subgroup equations for I_U show that comultiplication kills I
   modulo I in both factors. Inversion and the counit also preserve I. Thus Spec B
   is a closed subgroup of finite type, and its quotient maps prove minimality.
4. After every field extension B injects into the product of the extended B_S, so
   it is reduced. Idempotents in all these connected factors have equal values,
   as evaluation at the common identity agrees. Injectivity makes every idempotent
   zero or one; the connectedness criterion proves geometric connectedness.
5. Galois stability of F and minimality imply that each conjugate of Spec B equals
   Spec B as an embedded subgroup. Its ideal is therefore stable under the canonical
   semilinear action. Apply lem-sfb-galois-descent-affine-subgroups to descend it
   uniquely to L. The descended coordinate quotient is affine and finitely generated.
6. Faithfully flat surjectivity on spectra descends connectedness. Using
   lem-weil-common-extension-fields, compare K and an algebraic closure in a common
   overfield. A basis of O(L) shows that the map from its algebraic-closure extension
   into that common extension is injective. The latter is reduced by step 4, so
   lem-trf-geometric-reducedness-algebraic-closure-test gives geometric reducedness
   of L. Finally lem-sfb-geometrically-reduced-group-smooth gives smoothness.
7. Two minimal subgroups become equal over K; the uniqueness clause of
   lem-sfb-galois-descent-affine-subgroups identifies their inclusions over k.
   For the empty family minimality gives the identity subgroup over K, and descent
   uniqueness gives the identity subgroup over k. No commutativity or torsion is used.
-/
theorem galoisStableAffineLine_generated_subgroup
    (k K : Type u) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] [IsSepClosure k K]
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]
    (G : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj G] [IsAffine G.left]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType G.hom] [QuasiCompact G.hom] [Smooth G.hom]
    (F : Set
      ((Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj
        (StandardGroupSchemes.additive k) ⟶
       (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).obj G))
    (hpointed : ∀ f ∈ F,
      (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).map
        η[StandardGroupSchemes.additive k] ≫ f =
        (Over.pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k K)))).map η[G])
    (hstable : ∀ (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K), ∀ f ∈ F, ∃ f' ∈ F,
      f'.left ≫ baseChangeMap G.hom (specAlgEquivOver σ) =
        baseChangeMap (StandardGroupSchemes.additive k).hom (specAlgEquivOver σ) ≫
          f.left) :
    ∃ (L : Over (Spec (.of k))) (gL : GrpObj L) (i : L ⟶ G),
      @IsClosedSubgroupScheme k _ L G gL _ i ∧
      IsAffine L.left ∧ LocallyOfFiniteType L.hom ∧ QuasiCompact L.hom ∧
      Smooth L.hom ∧ ConnectedSpace L.left ∧
      IsAffineLineGeneratedAfterBaseChange k K G F L i ∧
      (∀ (L' : Over (Spec (.of k))) (gL' : GrpObj L') (i' : L' ⟶ G),
        @IsClosedSubgroupScheme k _ L' G gL' _ i' →
        IsAffine L'.left → LocallyOfFiniteType L'.hom → QuasiCompact L'.hom →
        Smooth L'.hom → ConnectedSpace L'.left →
        IsAffineLineGeneratedAfterBaseChange k K G F L' i' →
        ∃ e : L' ≅ L, e.hom ≫ i = i') ∧
      (F = ∅ → ∃ e : L ≅ 𝟙_ (Over (Spec (.of k))), e.hom ≫ η[G] = i) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
